      "evidence": "The idea as written is a monitoring/tracking software tool for deadlines, audit dates, and rule changes. It does not describe filing on the customer's behalf, holding a license, or handling protected health data. Selling monitoring software to regulated customers does not trigger R001. Some competitors (e.g., Copliancy, Filejet, Harbor Compliance) offer optional 'managed services' that do file on behalf of clients, but that is not what A02 describes.",
